     "\n\n\n\n\n\n\n<div>\n<font face=\"Verdana\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-size:9pt\">\n<div>Hi, </div>\n<div><font face=\"Calibri\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"> </span></font></div>\n<div>I have loaded ggplot 0.9.0, and wanted to plot some older scripts that have worded using the older verison of ggplot. </div>\n<div> </div>\n<div>For instance I cannot now control the order for which the geom_area is stacking the data, before I only made the change like this:</div>\n<div><font face=\"Calibri\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"> </span></font></div>\n<div>Data$variable &lt;- factor(Data$variable, levels = c(“1”,etc) )</div>\n<div><font face=\"Calibri\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"> </span></font></div>\n<div>But now the levels do change but geom_area does not recognize the change</div>\n<div><font face=\"Calibri\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"> </span></font></div>\n<div>Regards</div>\n<div><font face=\"Calibri\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"> </span></font></div>\n<div style=\"margin-bottom:10pt\"><font face=\"Calibri\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"><br>\n\n<font face=\"Verdana\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt\">Serdar Akin<br>\n\n____________________________________________________________<br>\n\n</span></font></span></font></div>\n<div style=\"margin-bottom:10pt\"><font face=\"Calibri\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"> </span></font></div>\n<div><font face=\"Calibri\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"> </span></font></div>\n<div><font face=\"Calibri\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"font-size:11pt\"> </span></font></div>\n</span></font>\n</div>\n\n"
